# backup-widget data collectors.
#
# Three tiers, because they cost very different amounts:
#   1m   local log parsing only - no cloud calls, no filesystem walks
#   5m   one Dropbox listing call, for byte-accurate mirror progress
#   1h   one quota call per provider
#   6h   all three clouds plus a du over every dataset
#
# Per-second figures do NOT come from cron: the page queries rclone's rc server
# directly, in-process, which is the only way to move like a CPU graph.
* * * * * bash /boot/config/plugins/backup-widget/scripts/duplicacy-status.sh >/dev/null 2>&1
* * * * * bash /boot/config/plugins/backup-widget/scripts/rclone-live.sh >/dev/null 2>&1
*/5 * * * * bash /boot/config/plugins/backup-widget/scripts/rclone-progress.sh >/dev/null 2>&1
5 */6 * * * bash /boot/config/plugins/backup-widget/scripts/duplicacy-coverage.sh >/dev/null 2>&1
7 */6 * * * bash /boot/config/plugins/backup-widget/scripts/backup-inventory.sh >/dev/null 2>&1
10 */6 * * * bash /boot/config/plugins/backup-widget/scripts/backup-history.sh >/dev/null 2>&1
# Hourly is right for quota: it is three API calls, and free space does not move
# fast enough to warrant more. Offset from the 6-hourly tier so a quota check never
# lands in the same minute as a coverage pass competing for the same providers.
17 * * * * bash /boot/config/plugins/backup-widget/scripts/cloud-quota.sh >/dev/null 2>&1
